[2025-11-24 11:20:49,444] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca653b1520537c7ac5b06'), 'title': 'The Battle at 25 Northumberland Road: A 3D Scholarly Edition', 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca653b1520537c7ac5b05'), 'dc': {'title': 'The Battle at 25 Northumberland Road: A 3D Scholarly Edition', 'creator': ['Susan Schreibman', 'Kelly Gillikin Schoueri', 'John Kaulakis', 'Luca Moine', 'Sandra Martinez Böhme'], 'contributor': ['Billy Donnelly', 'Brian Hughes'], 'institution': ['Maastricht University'], 'abstract': 'This 3D Scholarly Edition utilises a 3D reconstruction to contextualise and\nnarrate the events focusing the first building the British troops (The\nSherwood Foresters) encountered on the afternoon of 26 April 1916 on their\nmarch into the city centre. The building was held by Irish Volunteers Michael\nMalone and James Grace of C Company, 3rd Battalion of the Dublin Brigade of\nIrish Volunteers.  Sources agree that the battle began around 12.30 on\nWednesday afternoon as the Volunteers shot at oncoming British troops. The\ntime the building fell is contested as sources provide varying accounts. ', 'subject': ['Irish History', 'Easter Rising', 'British History', 'World War I'], 'coverage': {'period': '1916-04-24 / 1916-04-27', 'place': 'Dublin, Ireland'}, 'language': ['English'], 'rights': {'holder': 'Susan Schreibman', 'license': 'CC - BY - NC - ND'}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-28T12-20-04', 'pubNum': 1}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,444] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,445] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca657b1520537c7ac5b08'), 'title': 'Diaconie Weeshuis', 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca657b1520537c7ac5b07'), 'dc': {'title': 'Diaconie Weeshuis', 'creator': ['Tijm Lanjouw'], 'contributor': [], 'institution': ['4D Research Lab/ASACA/JCQ'], 'abstract': 'In the latter half of the 17th century, the Diaconie Weeshuis, an Amsterdam\norphanage managed by a protestant church, proudly overlooked the Amstel\nriver. It was located on former ‘Vlooienburg’, an island constructed in the\nAmstel river for urban expansion around 1600. The orphanage was constructed\nin 1656, after the plague epidemic of 1654-55 which had turned many children\nto orphanhood. It was sited on a previously unbuilt quay area on the edge of\nVlooienburg. To make space for this large building, a new strip of land had\nto be reclaimed from the Amstel river. This building stood here for 230 years\nbefore it got replaced by a new orphanage building in Neogothic style in\n1888. Neither of the two buildings have survived, and especially for the\nolder building there are only few remaining visual sources. This 3D\nreconstruction for the first time synthesises these sources into a model of\nthis lost piece of architecture of Amsterdam.', 'subject': ['Diaconie Weeshuis', 'Amsterdam', 'Vlooienburg', 'Virtual Reconstruction'], 'coverage': {'period': '1625 / 1890', 'place': 'Amsterdam, Netherlands'}, 'language': ['English'], 'rights': {'holder': '4D Research Lab', 'license': 'CC - BY '}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-27T11-06-55', 'pubNum': 1}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,445] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,446] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca658b1520537c7ac5b0a'), 'title': 'MVRDV - The Hannover Expo 2000', 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca658b1520537c7ac5b09'), 'dc': {'title': 'MVRDV - The Hannover Expo 2000', 'creator': ['Brittany Brighouse', 'Ania Molenda'], 'contributor': [], 'institution': ['Het Nieuwe Instituut'], 'abstract': 'The World Expo 2000 in Hannover was the first world exhibition to be held in\nthe 21st Century and the very first to ever be held in Germany. The main theme\nof Expo 2000 was sustainable development and bridging the gap between nature\nand culture. Most of the pavilions at the Expo reflected on the relationship\nbetween nature and culture and The Netherlands’ pavilion designed by\narchitectural firm MVRDV was no exception. Six stacked stereotypical ‘Dutch’\nlandscapes formed the building’s structure. This architectural experiment\nsought to showcase the possibilities of utilizing space as population density\nincreases as well as exploring the concept of ‘new nature’: a mix of technology\nand the natural. This 3D edition utilizes the 3D model made by MVRDV and\nother born-digital archival material to detail their vision of sustainable\narchitecture. ', 'subject': ['Dutch design', 'architecture', 'sustainable development'], 'coverage': {'period': '2000 / 2100', 'place': 'Hannover, Germany'}, 'language': ['English'], 'rights': {'holder': 'MVRDV/Het Nieuwe Instituut', 'license': 'CC - BY - NC - ND'}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-27T11-06-26', 'pubNum': 1}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,446] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,446] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca65ab1520537c7ac5b0c'), 'title': 'Maarten van Bommel op Bank', 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca65ab1520537c7ac5b0b'), 'dc': {'title': 'Maarten van Bommel op Bank', 'creator': ['Hilde Janssen'], 'contributor': ['Shanou Basten-Janssen'], 'institution': ['Museum van Bommel van Dam'], 'abstract': "Maarten van Bommel op bank is a 3D edition of a ceramic sculpture made for\nMaarten van Bommel on the occaison of his birthday in 1989. The 3D model of\nthe sculpture is used as an opportunity to open the digital collection of\nModern Art in 3D by providing some background information on the collectors,\nMaarten and Reina van Bommel van Dam, as well as ellaborating on the artist's\nchoices within the sculpture. The sculpture is today displayed in the Museum\nvan Bommel van Dam in a period room replicating the Van Bommel van Dam\ncouple's sitting room. ", 'subject': ['modern art', 'sculpture', 'ceramic', 'Maarten van Bommel van Dam', 'Reina van Bommel van Dam'], 'coverage': {'period': '1989-05-09', 'place': 'Venlo, Limburg, The Netherlands'}, 'language': ['English', 'Dutch'], 'rights': {'holder': 'Museum van Bommel van Dam', 'license': 'CC - BY - NC - ND'}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-27T11-06-07', 'pubNum': 1}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,446] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,446] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca65eb1520537c7ac5b0e'), 'title': "Rembrandt's Birthplace", 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca65eb1520537c7ac5b0d'), 'dc': {'title': "Rembrandt's Birthplace", 'creator': ['PJ De Vos'], 'contributor': [], 'institution': ['Heritage Leiden (Erfgoed Leiden en Omstreken)'], 'abstract': 'The virtual edition is a presentation of the house of Rembrandt will walk you\nthrough the background, architecture and daily life of Leiden in the years\nafter the siege of Leiden by the Spanish in 1573. ', 'subject': ['Vernacular Architecture', 'Leiden', 'Rembrandt, Mill', 'Cityscape', 'History', 'Architecture', 'Archaeology'], 'coverage': {'period': '1573 / 1637', 'place': 'The Netherlands'}, 'language': ['English', 'Dutch'], 'rights': {'holder': 'Erfgoed Leiden en Omstreken; Mr. The Rich', 'license': 'CC-BY-ND'}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-27T11-06-38', 'pubNum': 1}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,447] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,447] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca662b1520537c7ac5b10'), 'title': 'Petrol Lamp - Safety and Hazards', 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca662b1520537c7ac5b0f'), 'dc': {'title': 'Petrol Lamp - Safety and Hazards', 'creator': ['Miriam Paloni', 'Kevin Raetsen', 'Kirstin Römer'], 'contributor': [], 'institution': ['Nederlands Mijnmuseum'], 'abstract': 'This edition is about the so-called petrol lamp, it’s advantages and\nthe danger it posed. In 1882, the German manufacturer Carl Wolf\ndeveloped the first petrol lamp with an integrated igniter and\nmagnetic lock. Compared to the existing mining lamps, that used to\nburn oil, the petrol lamp had several advantages, which made this\nlamp burn cleaner, brighter and safer.', 'subject': ['Petrol Lamp', 'Safety and Hazards', 'dangers in the mining industry'], 'coverage': {'period': 'Early Modern', 'place': 'TBD'}, 'language': ['English'], 'rights': {'holder': 'Nederlands Mijnmuseum', 'license': 'CC - BY - NC - ND'}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-27T11-05-27', 'pubNum': 2}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,447] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,447] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca665b1520537c7ac5b11'), 'title': 'Attachable Helmet Lamp - A Relief for the Miner', 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca662b1520537c7ac5b0f'), 'dc': {'title': 'Attachable Helmet Lamp - A Relief for the Miner', 'creator': ['Miriam Paloni', 'Kevin Raetsen', 'Kirstin Römer'], 'contributor': [], 'institution': ['Nederlands Mijnmuseum'], 'abstract': 'This edition is about the so-called cap or helmet lamp. From the\nmid-1950s, the cap lamp was the most commonly used lamp in the\nunderground mining industry. The lamp brought a welcome relief to\nthe miner where comfort was concerned. The cap lamp was easier to\nhandle, lighter and more portable than earlier types of mining\nlamps. ', 'subject': ['helmet lamp', 'attachable helmet lamp', 'cap lamp'], 'coverage': {'period': 'Early Modern', 'place': 'TBD'}, 'language': ['English'], 'rights': {'holder': 'Nederlands Mijnmuseum', 'license': 'CC - BY - NC - ND'}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-27T11-05-16', 'pubNum': 1}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,448] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,448] DEBUG in messages: YYY edition={'_id': ObjectId('64eca667b1520537c7ac5b13'), 'title': 'The Church of Our Lady and its Claustral Belt', 'projectId': ObjectId('64eca667b1520537c7ac5b12'), 'dc': {'title': 'The Church of Our Lady and its Claustral Belt', 'creator': ['Eric Wetzels'], 'contributor': ['Kelly Gillikin Schoueri'], 'institution': ['Municipality of Maastricht'], 'abstract': 'The Onze Lieve Vrouweplein, or Church of Our Lady, is one of two prominent\nsquares in the city of Maastricht that has witnessed 2000 years of history.\nIt was once the setting of a major religious chapter for the city where\nchapter lords lived and maintained the buildings and community functions of\nthe  religious complexes. This 3D edition reveals some of that history\nthrough an annotated model of the French military maquette from 1748 and two\nguided tours that walk through the broad historical moments the square has\nwitnessed as well as historical contextualization to the naming of the\nstreets surrounding the square. ', 'subject': ['Maastricht', 'religious chapters', 'chapter lords', 'Church of Our Lady', 'Onze Lieve Vrouweplein', 'Claustral Belt'], 'coverage': {'period': 'Roman era to Modern Time', 'place': 'Maastricht, Limburg, The Netherlands '}, 'language': ['English', 'Dutch'], 'rights': {'holder': 'Municipality of Maastricht', 'license': 'CC - BY - NC - ND'}}, 'settings': {'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}, 'isPublished': True, 'lastPublished': '2024-03-27T11-05-53', 'pubNum': 1}
[2025-11-24 11:20:49,448] DEBUG in messages: YYY editionSettings={'authorTool': {'name': 'voyager', 'version': '0.29.1', 'sceneFile': 'scene.svx.json'}}
