ar_url': 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22783547?v=4', 'gravatar_id': '', 'url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/gjcope', 'followers_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/followers', 'following_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/following{/other_user}', 'gists_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/gists{/gist_id}', 'starred_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/starred{/owner}{/repo}', 'subscriptions_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/subscriptions', 'organizations_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/orgs', 'repos_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/repos', 'events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/events{/privacy}', 'received_events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/gjcope/received_events', 'type': 'User', 'user_view_type': 'public', 'site_admin': False}, 'content_type': 'application/x-zip-compressed', 'state': 'uploaded', 'size': 10001427, 'digest': None, 'download_count': 8, 'created_at': '2023-11-30T18:53:37Z', 'updated_at': '2023-11-30T18:53:42Z', 'browser_download_url': 'https://github.com/Smithsonian/dpo-voyager/releases/download/v0.35.0/voyager-tools-v0.35.0.zip'}], 'tarball_url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/Smithsonian/dpo-voyager/tarball/v0.35.0', 'zipball_url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/Smithsonian/dpo-voyager/zipball/v0.35.0', 'body': 'Changelog:\r\n\r\n**New Features:**\r\n* Materials imported as Three.js "MeshPhysicalMaterial" will now respect those properties and use a derivative of that material rather than falling back to the standard material in all cases.\r\n  * The new material (UberPBRAdvMaterial) still supports the same standard extended features (normal view, x-ray, cut plane. etc.) but opens up support for advanced glTF PBR properties like transmission and translucency.\r\n  * This also allowed the uberPBRShader to be updated to become more in line with the current Three.js version which will ease future updates. \r\n\r\n**Bug Fixes:**\r\n* Annotation materials are now excluded from tone mapping\r\n'}
